description: |-
  USC-II skeletal mechanism (run "usc_ii" reduction, flame-repaired aggressive member).

  Parent: USC-II, 111 species / 784 reactions (tasks/usc_ii/parent.yaml), unmodified.
  This file: 63 species / 461 reactions.  Construction: (1) species elimination from the parent by
  validation-driven greedy removal on a 77-case ignition probe set (tolerance box mean/p95/max
  |ln(tau/tau_parent)| = 0.25/0.55/1.30), which produced the 50-species member; (2) FLAME-INFORMED
  REPAIR - the thirteen parent species CH2, CH, C2H, HCCO, CH3CHO, CH3CO, CO2, pC3H4, aC3H4, C4H2,
  CH2OH, CH2*, nC4H5 were added back (scripts/mk_backadd.py) because the 50-species member's laminar
  flame speeds collapsed by 78-97 % on every fuel tested; CH2OH/CH2* also restore the missing
  CH2OH branch of the methanol sub-mechanism that the 50-species member had lost.
  No rate parameter, thermodynamic or transport datum is modified anywhere; every reaction and every
  species is the parent's own.
  PROVENANCE CAVEAT: the probe set used for step (1) was built with the wrong mixture convention
  (X_O2 = 1/phi); that acceptance evidence is void and is not the basis of any accuracy claim here.
  Held-out accuracy (792-case ignition matrix; parent reference results/ref_ign_matrix.csv):
    mean |ln(tau/tau_parent)| = 0.111, p95 = 0.444, max = 0.697, 9.9 % of cases above 35 % error.
  Laminar flame speeds (phi = 1, 300 K, 1 atm, 11 fuels, vs the container parent): mean |dSu/Su| =
  4.1 %, max 11.5 % (propene); worst fuels also include n-butane (-9.4 %) and benzene (-7.4 %).
  For comparison the 50-species precursor has mean 87 % / max 97 % on the same cases.
  Cost: 461/784 = 59 % of the parent's reactions; wall time per ignition case ~0.3x the parent.
  Files: results/red50_bA.yaml (this file before annotation), results/local_flame_bA_full.csv,
  results/lv_ba_red50_bA_ign.csv.

